{
  "kind": "tea",
  "teaId": "zelophehad",
  "text": "Five sisters walked up to Moses, the priest, the princes and the entire assembly, and changed inheritance law.\n\nNumbers twenty-seven. Their names are Mahlah, Noah, Hoglah, Milcah and Tirzah, and Scripture lists every single one.\n\nTheir father died in the wilderness with no sons. Under the rules as they stood, land moved through sons. So his name and his portion just vanish.\n\nAnd these five women do not petition quietly.\n\nThey stood before Moses, and before Eleazar the priest, and before the princes and all the congregation, at the door of the tabernacle.\n\nThat is the entire leadership of the nation, plus everybody else. And five sisters walk up and make a legal argument.\n\n\"Why should the name of our father be done away from among his family, because he hath no son? Give unto us therefore a possession among the brethren of our father.\"\n\nAnd Moses does not rule on it. He doesn't wing it. \"And Moses brought their cause before the Lord.\"\n\nAnd the answer comes back.\n\n\"The daughters of Zelophehad speak right.\"\n\nSpeak right. God agreed with them, on the record, and the inheritance law of Israel was rewritten because five women asked.",
